cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its findings, please cite it as below."
title: "Jev Board Game: belief as a primitive for social-deduction games"
abstract: >-
  A research testbed and analysis harness that instruments social-deduction games
  (Undercover, with Werewolf and Avalon planned) with a calibrated System-One model
  (Jev, by TypeSafe). Each agent's suspicion is obtained as a typed, natively
  calibrated probability distribution rather than probed from an autoregressive
  language model's verbalized confidence. Every Jev judgement is logged per round
  and scored for calibration (expected calibration error, Brier score) and
  belief-trajectory dynamics against known ground truth, and can be replayed in a
  terminal or self-contained web "God's-eye" viewer.
type: software
